# Line endings. The repository stores text files with LF. Git converts them
# to your platform's line ending on checkout and back to LF on commit, so a
# Windows checkout (CRLF) and a Linux or macOS one (LF) both show a clean
# status, whatever each machine's core.autocrlf is set to.
* text=auto

# Files that run inside Linux containers keep LF everywhere.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Binary files: never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
